    "updated_at": "2021-04-03T23:56:52Z",
    "body": "This would be great. It's something I have in my current prompt (home grown) and I just spent a while trying to figure out how to get it working in starship.\r\n\r\nEdit: Managed to work around this in bash for now… Mileage may vary for other shells so it would still be great to have a starship solution.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[character]\r\nsuccess_symbol = '\\$'\r\n```\r\n\r\nfrom https://tldp.org/HOWTO/Bash-Prompt-HOWTO/bash-prompt-escape-sequences.html\r\n> `\\$`: if the effective UID is 0, a #, otherwise  a $",
    "author_association": "NONE",
