    "created_at": "2022-11-18T23:52:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-12T07:41:06Z",
    "body": "## Solution\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Modify `starship.toml` config in user mode\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nvi ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n[character]\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[\\\\$](green bold)\"\r\nerror_symbol = \"[\\\\$](red bold)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Switch to the root\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nsudo -s\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Install starship under the root\r\n\r\n...like you would do under the normal user, e.g. install the starship binary according to the installation guide and add `eval $(starship init bash)` into `/root/.profile`.\r\n\r\nThe user starship binary can be used:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\neval \"$(/home/<user>/.cargo/bin/starship init bash)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Step 4: Modify `starship.toml` under the root\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# /home/root/.config/starship.toml\r\nvi ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n[character]\r\nsuccess_symbol = \"[#](green bold)\"\r\nerror_symbol = \"[#](red bold)\"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
