    "body": "Thanks @fadeevab - it didn't work for me on zsh/macos.\r\n\r\nActually, it initially didn't work on bash/linux either, until I created a ~root/.bashrc invocation of starship - so that may be a step missing in the above comment (or perhaps starship was in /etc/profile* or something similar)\r\n\r\nHowever, on macos the root shell is /bin/sh and AFAIK that only executes ~/.profile on login shells (so sudo -i might work), and doesn't have any other startup file; also sh isn't supported by starship anyway.",
