    "body": "@jimcheetham yeah, the missing step is that after switching to root, you have to install starship first under the **root**, like you would do under the normal user, (e.g. add `eval $(starship init bash)` into `/root/.profile`). The comment was not supposed to be like a full guide :)) Anyways, I will update it.\r\n\r\nAlso, the user starship binary can be used:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\neval \"$(/home/<user>/.cargo/bin/starship init bash)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nUPD: Updated comment (aka \"guide\"): https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2421#issuecomment-1320668538",
