    "body": "I miss a such a feature as well. If root should have almost the same config as the user, it's simpler to copy the config, instead of maintaining slightly different versions.\n\nMy current workaround that allows for different styling as well:\n```\nformat = \"[...] ${custom.user}${custom.root}\"\n\n[custom.user]\nformat = '[\\$]($style)'\nwhen = 'whoami | grep -vq root'\nstyle = 'bold blue'\n\n[custom.root]\nformat = '[#]($style)'\nwhen = 'whoami | grep -q root'\nstyle = 'bold red'\n```\n\nI think `style_root` could be useful in all modules, not just `Username`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
